# Local development environment.
#
# NOT COMMITTED and never should be: .gitignore covers it. Vercel holds the
# real values for production and preview, and NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at
# BUILD time, so a key set only in Vercel works there and never locally.
#
# The MapTiler key is NOT missing from the platform: the founder verified it
# is set in Vercel for production and preview on 23 September. This file is
# only how a sandbox gets one locally. Without it the map renders the
# non-commercial OpenStreetMap CARTO fallback, which is a local-only
# appearance and not a product defect.

NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY=

# ----------------------------------------------------------- Push, locally
#
# The two variables below are the whole of Web Push, and Web Push is the one
# transport that needs nobody and costs nothing:
#
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#
# Paste the public half into the first and the private half into the second,
# in `.env.local`, which is NOT committed. Then follow
# docs/push/FIRST_NOTIFICATION.md, which is about a minute end to end.
#
# SUPPLIED BY: nobody, you generate them. COSTS: nothing.
#
# GENERATE THE PAIR ONCE AND KEEP IT. Every subscription a browser makes is
# bound to the public half, so a new pair silently kills every device already
# enrolled. The same pair belongs in Vercel for production, and in Vault.
#
# Android (FCM) and iOS (APNs) need credentials only the founder can create,
# and one of them costs 99 USD a year. Neither is needed to see a notification
# arrive. They are in `.env.example` with who supplies them and what they
# cost, one comment per variable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
